{"status":"completed","summary":"Built and validated the replicated CORP.EXAMPLE Samba AD environment across all four nodes. Authentication, redundant DNS, Kerberos, engineering-share access, controller failover, and restart persistence are proven.","actions_performed":["Provisioned node1 and node2 as replicated Samba AD controllers bound to 10.100.194.0/24.","Created engineering and its member infrasetuser, with replication verified.","Joined node3 as a member server and published the writable engineering share with the required welcome.txt.","Joined node4 and created /root/corp-user.env with mode 0600.","Demonstrated authentication, DNS, and SMB access with either controller unavailable.","Removed temporary credential staging files.","Rebooted every node individually and verified changed boot IDs and role/data recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Replicated CORP.EXAMPLE controllers on the dedicated identity network","command_ids":["cmd-f3226ba46a0b42af","cmd-8c2acc3406c5419e","cmd-52d1e60e446b4d6e","cmd-9828670ebc4b4454"],"summary":"Both controllers are active, publish LDAP/Kerberos through 10.100.194.10/11, have zero database errors, and report zero replication failures."},{"requirement":"engineering group containing infrasetuser","command_ids":["cmd-c348806b50364015","cmd-5851f8a029d04535"],"summary":"Shows object creation, membership, and replicated visibility on node2."},{"requirement":"node3 engineering share, required content, and member write access","command_ids":["cmd-5d3ba1ad86334c70","cmd-6bb6ec26c5f041d6","cmd-8e4a591fc56c408b","cmd-8b5b589339f24030"],"summary":"Shows healthy domain trust, SMB bound to 10.100.194.12, welcome.txt containing infraset-samba, and successful authenticated write round trips."},{"requirement":"Joined node4 with protected credential environment","command_ids":["cmd-9b7393c91bff49b8","cmd-665580b3d92a4c5b","cmd-3dab81a3e078481f"],"summary":"The client join and trust are healthy; /root/corp-user.env is root-owned mode 0600 and persists without exposing its password."},{"requirement":"Availability while node1 controller is down","command_ids":["cmd-741cd782df6d40fa","cmd-37ba1e80500142dd","cmd-e8745e64ac044938"],"summary":"With node1 stopped, node2 provided DNS and fresh Kerberos authentication while SMB read/write remained available; node1 was then restored."},{"requirement":"Availability while node2 controller is down","command_ids":["cmd-f2f6a454a83141ba","cmd-aa293d018b2a4419","cmd-61e2b2f81719452a","cmd-7009f73357104d03"],"summary":"With node2 stopped, node1 provided DNS and a fresh TGT, SMB read/write succeeded, and client trust/password authentication rediscovered node1; node2 was restored."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart persistence","command_ids":["cmd-05a360b5c7f844ec","cmd-289c93e67a36438b","cmd-f489b04c4bea445e","cmd-ec38f5ce23884c67"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, boot ID change, and recovered AD/DNS/data state."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node2 restart persistence","command_ids":["cmd-11e1a3c7eb0444ad","cmd-ce9cf114459d4edd","cmd-3dbdcf6fb2084b9d","cmd-0665bbd373974aae","cmd-9828670ebc4b4454"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, boot ID change, and recovered controller/database/replication state."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node3 restart persistence","command_ids":["cmd-61ab3d4c204d478b","cmd-fc6cafc486e74116","cmd-8dae3bc3ea264ce3","cmd-72e38507e82f449f","cmd-fbda15841c234e39"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, boot ID change, restored trust/share data, and authenticated post-reboot SMB write."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node4 restart persistence","command_ids":["cmd-1a2816ee57ac4642","cmd-a665438bec84453e","cmd-b28df5854e5e4a71","cmd-3dab81a3e078481f"],"summary":"Healthy baseline, reboot acknowledgement, boot ID change, persistent credentials, restored trust, fresh Kerberos authentication, DNS, and SMB read/write."}]}
